      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{-12-9x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=-12-9x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{-12-9x}\\,\\text{d}x & =1\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}u\\right) \\\\ & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\ & =-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-12-9x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
